      "problem": "A soap dispenser has a volume of $1$ pint. What is this volume in cups?",
      "worked_solution": "A table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\textrm{gal}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{gal} = 8\\,\\textrm{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\textrm{pt}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{pt} = 2\\,\\textrm{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\textrm{cup} = 8\\,\\textrm{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\textrm{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\textrm{pint}$ is equivalent to $2\\,\\textrm{cups}.$",
